FitHub Phase 3 focused evidence — DEF-006 / FR-33 notification preferences
Execution date: 2026-10-22 (Europe/Berlin)
Environment: Local Docker Compose; Angular http://localhost:4040; API http://localhost:8080; PostgreSQL 18
Test account: Active Member, active-member@fithub.demo, synthetic active-Membership development account
Administrator used for the qualifying event: phase2.manual-admin@fithub.test, synthetic Administrator
Qualifying event: Fault report 982b7ca3-f703-4160-965c-eb42c9853a20 for BIKE-001 / Exercise bike

Preconditions
- Active Member was authenticated and /notification-preferences was reachable from Member navigation.
- All six supported optional categories initially existed and were enabled.
- The evaluator password was read from ignored development configuration and is not recorded here.

Focused steps and results
1. Opened /notification-preferences in the browser.
   Expected: human-readable switches for categories with real backend triggers.
   Actual: Class reminders, Equipment report updates, Membership renewal, Personal records, Streak risk and Training reminders were shown.
2. Disabled Equipment report updates through the authenticated current-Member preferences API and refreshed the page.
   Expected: the choice persists and the browser shows the switch off.
   Actual: PostgreSQL stored Enabled=false and the refreshed switch displayed off.
3. Created the synthetic BIKE-001 UnusualSound report and changed it to UnderReview as the Administrator.
   Expected: no new fault-status notification while the category is disabled.
   Actual: zero notifications existed for deduplication key fault:982b7ca3-f703-4160-965c-eb42c9853a20:UnderReview.
4. Re-enabled Equipment report updates and changed the report to Scheduled.
   Expected: one future qualifying notification is created.
   Actual: the Member Notifications page displayed “Fault report updated — Your report for Exercise bike is now Scheduled.”
5. Processed the same Scheduled event again.
   Expected: stable deduplication keeps one notification.
   Actual: PostgreSQL contained exactly one row for fault:982b7ca3-f703-4160-965c-eb42c9853a20:Scheduled.
6. Refreshed the preferences page.
   Expected: the re-enabled value remains stored.
   Actual: PostgreSQL stored Enabled=true and the refreshed browser switch displayed on.

Database verification
- NotificationPreferences has one row per user/category enforced by a unique index.
- FaultReportStatusUpdate persisted false during suppression and true after re-enabling.
- Disabled event count: 0. Re-enabled repeated event count: 1.
- Existing notifications remained present in the Member notification list.

Automated verification relevant to this feature
- Backend unit tests: 114 passed, 0 failed.
- PostgreSQL integration tests: 91 passed, 0 failed, including defaults, current-user ownership, invalid category rejection, suppression, re-enable, persistence, retained history, deduplication and idempotent seeding.
- Angular tests: 139 passed across 44 files, including loading, save, failure, reload and Member-only navigation visibility.
- Angular production build: passed; only pre-existing simulator stylesheet budget warnings remain.

Decision: PASS
Limitation: The six toggles correspond only to categories with implemented backend triggers. Security/payment notices are not part of this optional enum and therefore cannot be disabled here.
